  "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{24}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+x]}_{0}^{1}+{[\\frac{1}{48}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}+1]-[\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{4}+0])+\\frac{1}{48}[{5}^{2}-{1}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{5}{4})+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{16}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
